Z||000000||AgaricX||11-30-2001||04:58 AM||||Hey... does anyone know if anyone has ever thought about manufacturing the glass clip part of the '89 Fiero concept car for application on our notchbacks?  I think it would look AWESOME.  It probably wouldnt be THAT bad for a glass shop.  IF it's even glass...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/fiero891.jpg"> <P>I mean COME ON!!! Am I alone in the fact that I think that that would be the most perfect compromise between the fastback and a notchback??  I have my green machine and an ugly SE that I'd love to put somthing like that on.  (after the greuling bodywork is done)<P>While I'm at it... I need a HIGH RES pic of the '89 if anyone has it.  640x480 at least... 1024x768 if anyone has it.<P>l8r<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indy-2M4||11-30-2001||05:19 AM||||Good thought, but I think the butt end of the car would need to be longer for one. And the deck lid, well....that goes along with the extended rear, I mean that heat from the engine is going to go up into the glass hatch. If the car could somehow be modified for this, I think it might look decent.<P>------------------<BR>F.K.A. KathyHL<BR>Southwestern Ohio Fiero Association<BR>http:\\sofa.iwarp.com<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://sofa.iwarp.com/IndyFiero2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pyric||11-30-2001||06:43 AM||||I don't know... I like it and everything, but I think the concept lost too much of the Fiero body style and bears a closer resemblance to a firebird.<P>If you're really dying to do it, you could probably steal the hatch back off of a firebird or camaro.  Mounting it would be a different story.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||11-30-2001||06:59 AM||||It's not a glass hatch like on a Firebird or Camaro - the sail panels are glass, and the trailing edge wraps over just a bit towards the center of the car - it still has a vertical back glass and exposed horizontal decklid like all the other Fieros. <P>The appearance of a glass hatch in the above photos is an optical illusion.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000004||kslish||11-30-2001||07:08 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indy-2M4:<BR><B>I mean that heat from the engine is going to go up into the glass hatch. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It isn't a glass hatch, they are just sail panels that give the apearance of a hatch from the sides.  See below (you can see that the rear is still open):<P> <IMG SRC="http://homepage.mac.com/fieroinfo/images/fiero892.jpg"> <P>Ken S.<P><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
